  "text": "The group adopted several hardware decisions: drop speech recognition to reduce cost and complexity; keep the LCD display as the central screen for navigation and status; use one integrated button for all functions; and switch to two integrated scroll-wheel push-buttons while dropping all other push-buttons. There was a proposal to drop the 1-9 keypad in favor of up/down arrows and a menu for navigation. Budget is within reach after reductions, and the team will continue with the current plan; the hand dynamo option was deemed not viable and will not be pursued. Open problems include questionnaire scope clarification, budget constraints threatening features with high price sensitivity, concerns that dropping the keypad may hinder usability, the cost impact of two integrated scroll-wheel push-buttons, ongoing color strategy trade-offs, the essential role of maintaining the LCD display, and the potential impact of removing speech recognition on user experience.",
